WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.470
Lamp for reps. Part three: files and stages.

2
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:10.840
Every merchant who applies becomes a file. Files move left to right, one stage at a time.

3
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.220
New. The application came in. Nobody has reviewed it yet.

4
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.950
Reviewing. You have the file, and you're checking it.

5
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:23.460
Docs needed. You're waiting on bank statements or ID.

6
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.010
Submitted. The file went to one or more funders.

7
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.450
Offers ready. At least one offer is in front of the merchant.

8
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.780
Accepted. The merchant picked an offer.

9
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.350
Closing. The funder is doing its final checks.

10
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.890
Funded. The money went out.

11
00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:51.060
Three stages end a file. Declined: no funder would take it. Withdrawn: the merchant walked. Closed: archived.

12
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:59.820
To move a file, change the stage on its card. It jumps to the new column, and the change goes on the file's timeline.

13
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:07.750
Some stages fill in on their own. Sending a file to funders stamps it as sent, and recording the funding marks it funded.

14
00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.520
Files nobody owns yet show up on everyone's board.

15
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:17.230
Open one, and click Take this file. Now it's yours, and nobody else is working it.

16
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.010
Today watches your files for you. A file that's waiting too long shows up here with the next step.

17
00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:33.970
Move every file the same day something happens. The board is only as good as its stages.

18
00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.280
Next: working a file, start to finish.
